 authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.prop-strip-equiv"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.prop-strip-equiv"],"id":"long.prop-strip-equiv","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 12.4 (Terminal carry bounds are equivalent to half-membership)","locator":"Long record Proposition 12.4, p. 134, label prop:strip-equiv","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Consider finite sets $D\\subseteq\\{2,\\ldots,M\\}$ at arbitrarily large depths $M$ with\n$$\n|\\operatorname{ihc}(D,M-1)|\\le2\\lfloor\\sqrt M\\rfloor+4.\n$$\nThis is the exact terminal-strip condition. It is equivalent to $1/2\\in\\mathcal A$: the forward direction follows from the displayed finite-approximation estimate; for the converse, truncate an achieving support at $M=k^2$ and apply Lemma 2.6. Thus constant $4$ already suffices at cofinally many depths. The relaxed constant $6$ gives a bound at every depth, using $\\sqrt M\\le\\lfloor\\sqrt M\\rfloor+1$, but that relaxation is not needed for the cofinal statement.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-strip-equiv","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.prop-strip-equiv","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-strip-equiv%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_relaxed_constant_six_every_depth%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.prop-strip-equiv%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_relaxed_constant_six_every_depth%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_relaxed_constant_six